{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1553863-assassins","id":1553863,"title":"Assassins?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-16T16:20:23-07:00","id":1553863,"title":"Assassins?","content":"As I'm continuing to develop my mostly DC comics based setting, Ive been using the League of Assassins pretty often. Due to some crossover, they've adopted a lot of elements from Mortal Kombat and Assassin's Creed, so I've already given them a lot of depth and detail. But I haven't figured out the matter of Guild.<br /> <br /> One of the players started calling them the Assassin's Guild, and that brought the question to mind. While all Guilds likely had their leg breakers and killers, where might the Assassins fit in? Could they have been a Minor Guild, one that received either the full or partial Rite of Return? Or are they better off as a branch of an existing Guild? My initial idea was that they were a part of the Su-Menent, worshippers and priests of death who saw their murderous duty as sacred. Another obvious choice would be a more militant branch of the Maa-Kep. <br /> <br /> In my setting, the Assassins have broken into a handful of different factions. One is a slightly more heroic sort, straight out of Assassin's Creed. Another have become murderers for hire, notably the Lin Kuei. Others, like Kobra and Leviathan, lean more into terrorism and villainy. Each could be considered separate Cults, most having abandoned their Deathless master. But knowing their official Guild will help me figure out Guild Affinities and their relationship with Relics, most notably the Lazarus Pit. Ive avoided setting myself up for failure by treating the Pit as one of those multi-aspect Relics, a mixture of Regia and Uter formed from living and dead prokaryotes and nucleic acids set up via Nethian Architecture on a Fountain of Ma'at (Using roughly updated ideas from the Rio source book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T20:15:12-07:00","id":1553867,"title":"","content":"If you keep them as a branch of a Major Guild, I think it would be Maa-Kep. In the end, death to an Assassin is more a means to an end, even if it is somehow sacred. It has more to do with passing judgement in some level, which is a Maa-Kep thing.<br /> <br /> But I would make them a Minor Guild. They're something like the Kher-Minu in my opinion, and would work better as a non-guild personal service to the Shan'iatu back in Irem, probably expected to be completely loyal instead of having their own ideas in anything. Major Guilds are in many ways autonomous in their work, the Assassins wouldn't originally be so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}